                        "form": "доро́дны"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "155127f6-b5e4-4bdd-a213-16b35674f550",
                        "entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "доро́днее"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9fa0e5bc-890a-4a0b-82af-796f9a2c0467",
                        "entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "доро́дней"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6bd502a3-6533-3cd6-9728-72618d81c3b8",
                        "entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "· имеющий крупное, плотное телосложение; полный, тучный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "о человеке или животном"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c6bb81c-1de3-4e8c-9580-1c559476e6a1",
                                "sense_id": "6bd502a3-6533-3cd6-9728-72618d81c3b8",
                                "text": "А вот настоящий бык: дороден, доволен и жвачку жуёт, а работает, словно воз сена прёт, пьёт по целому чану враз…"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6e1b2d62-ec50-4a18-97f3-8f97e98f0433",
                                "sense_id": "6bd502a3-6533-3cd6-9728-72618d81c3b8",
                                "text": "Я заметила, что все служащие женщины были дородны и важны, почти величественны."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8de7a099-d9ca-31ea-b6ae-c487a47e1efc",
                        "entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг. · имеющий большие размеры, большой объём; крупный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "о предметах"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "876b459c-79e1-38db-a2ad-9b2ce4d88b5c",
                        "entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "старин. способный, смелый, чести достойный"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "54932bc9-d96a-4cf2-bdc4-7ac39bfed110",
                                "sense_id": "876b459c-79e1-38db-a2ad-9b2ce4d88b5c",
                                "text": "Мы узнаём от Ибн-Фодлана, что в 922 году правил ими дородный царь Алмас, Владавец, сын Силки, который, вероятно, царствовал в исходе девятого и начале десятого века."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8093c202-2b9f-48eb-8401-84b4d20a6b42",
                                "sense_id": "876b459c-79e1-38db-a2ad-9b2ce4d88b5c",
                                "text": "По писанному, кто злословит царя, тот смертию да умрёт: государь наш дородный государь, разумный и счастливый, сидит он на своих государствах по благословению отца своего и правит государством сам, и против всех недругов стоять готов так же как отец, дед и прадед его."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8d2708b8-07cb-4688-9043-7421298f1447",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "portly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "portly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65bdae79-c1db-30df-aa64-54631c5be45c",
                                        "entry_id": "83572212-57e6-39a2-b140-e9fb33931379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somewhat fat, pudgy, overweight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "566c059a-b531-44cc-b61a-5bfa5d3b87ca",
                                                "sense_id": "65bdae79-c1db-30df-aa64-54631c5be45c",
                                                "text": "Indeed, the poor man has grown ten times as nervous as ever, since he has discovered, on such good authority, who the stout gentleman was. . . . He has anxiously endeavored to call up a recollection of what he saw of that portly personage; and has ever since kept a curious eye on all gentlemen of more than ordinary dimensions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40c654de-dd0c-447b-92f7-74c7d0a00f96",
                                                "sense_id": "65bdae79-c1db-30df-aa64-54631c5be45c",
                                                "text": "In the length he attains, and in his baleen, the Fin-back resembles the right whale, but is of a less portly girth, and a lighter colour, approaching to olive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1933d5fa-f54d-49a6-9900-631aaf08265f",
                                                "sense_id": "65bdae79-c1db-30df-aa64-54631c5be45c",
                                                "text": "His portly middle section, rising beyond like a small hill, heaved rhythmically."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8940cfb5-3e37-4981-a1fe-e7bb7d7ea43a",
                                                "sense_id": "65bdae79-c1db-30df-aa64-54631c5be45c",
                                                "text": "In Heavyweights, Tony Perkis (Ben Stiller) is a fitness guru who installs himself as the über-buff leader of Camp Hope, with the goal of helping portly youngsters shed their saggy stomachs and thunder thighs."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7eb4332c-8014-3f01-80fb-813ef20e760e",
                                        "entry_id": "83572212-57e6-39a2-b140-e9fb33931379",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a dignified bearing; handsome, imposing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c3be59f-6d2e-4e12-ab9e-cb41627d38bf",
                                                "sense_id": "7eb4332c-8014-3f01-80fb-813ef20e760e",
                                                "text": "He ſends this Souldans daughter rich and braue,\nTo be my Queene and portly Empereſſe, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7dbc655-a009-4fbc-bfae-83d2a62d5b2f",
                                                "sense_id": "7eb4332c-8014-3f01-80fb-813ef20e760e",
                                                "text": "Portly his person was, and much increast\nThrough his Heroicke grace and honourable gest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00784b1c-0773-4c95-85a0-6058446c0046",
                                                "sense_id": "7eb4332c-8014-3f01-80fb-813ef20e760e",
                                                "text": "Be studious well to imitate\nMy portly motion, mien, and gait"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "54e51d7d-87b3-4430-96b8-50793d1078eb",
                        "source_entry_id": "a2e16775-dc62-3950-aab3-25357cc131bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "burly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "burly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b392178-b173-3f31-8215-32aefdad854d",
                                        "entry_id": "fc41e599-444a-3010-adc8-06599081f4ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Large, well-built, and muscular."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "647f3a4a-6cac-4d05-bc58-295fc2a9135b",
                                                "sense_id": "6b392178-b173-3f31-8215-32aefdad854d",
                                                "text": "He’s a big, burly rugby player who works as a landscape gardener."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ee72439-d849-47b5-9270-8365916b7491",
                                                "sense_id": "6b392178-b173-3f31-8215-32aefdad854d",
                                                "text": "With no great disparity between them in point of years, they were, in every other respect, as unlike and far removed from each other as two men could well be. The one was soft-spoken, delicately made, precise, and elegant; the other, a burly square-built man, negligently dressed, rough and abrupt in manner, stern, and, in his present mood, forbidding both in look and speech."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7bc1f0fe-ee39-49d1-ba45-5fe7e5e3194f",
                                                "sense_id": "6b392178-b173-3f31-8215-32aefdad854d",
                                                "text": "She was frankly disappointed. For some reason she had expected to discover a burglar of one or another accepted type—either a dashing cracksman in full-blown evening dress, lithe, polished, pantherish, or a common yegg, a red-eyed, unshaven, burly brute in the rags and tatters of a tramp."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ce0d820-72d3-4ce5-8a7c-bb64545dbaf3",
                                                "sense_id": "6b392178-b173-3f31-8215-32aefdad854d",
                                                "text": "Yossarian responded to the thought by slipping away stealthily from the police and almost tripped over the feet of a burly woman of forty hastening across the intersection guiltily, darting furtive, vindictive glances behind her toward a woman of eighty with thick, bandaged ankles doddering after her in a losing pursuit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e880c21d-a03a-3f61-ae62-d7fe32c415b3",
                                        "entry_id": "fc41e599-444a-3010-adc8-06599081f4ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Great, amazing, unbelievable."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "British",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cc0298b9-d023-4fc3-bdca-8f8a7315952b",
                                                "sense_id": "e880c21d-a03a-3f61-ae62-d7fe32c415b3",
                                                "text": "That goal was burly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8be50a51-1176-41ea-bfca-76ae11d911ef",
                                                "sense_id": "e880c21d-a03a-3f61-ae62-d7fe32c415b3",
                                                "text": "Kimi Räikkönen is a burly Formula 1 driver."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "348f858f-fc04-32d1-a264-ea8dd50cb90f",
                                        "entry_id": "fc41e599-444a-3010-adc8-06599081f4ad",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of large magnitude, either good or bad, and sometimes both."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "977e6a7a-6863-4d44-a591-b804a0d308f2",
                                                "sense_id": "348f858f-fc04-32d1-a264-ea8dd50cb90f",
                                                "text": "That wave was burly! (i.e. large, dangerous and difficult to ride)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a66b32f-5ce9-405a-833d-b0c8c4879b5c",
                                                "sense_id": "348f858f-fc04-32d1-a264-ea8dd50cb90f",
                                                "text": "This hike is going to be burly, but worth it because there is good body surfing at that beach."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "burly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5151fbd3-dcf3-3aec-9c2b-11bbc2093d8d",
                                        "entry_id": "5487d052-738d-3d7d-a164-eeca3b6ef2a6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Full of burls or knots; knotty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
